---
import Head from "../components/Head.astro";
import ZoomableImage from "../components/ZoomableImage.astro";
---

<style>
  main {
    font-family: "Open Sans Variable", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #3a3a54;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 128px auto;
    padding: 0 16px;
  }

  h1 {
    text-align: center;
  }

  section {
    display: flex;
    column-gap: 64px;

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }

  section + section {
    margin-top: 64px;
  }

  section > * {
    flex: 1 0;
  }

  section > .text {
    padding-top: 12px;
  }

  .project-title {
    display: flex;
    column-gap: 8px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .project-info {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    row-gap: 8px;
  }

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .tag {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid #eee;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>

<Head title="Linear" />

<main>
  <h1>Hello, Linear Team!</h1>
  <section>
    <h2>When I first met Linear</h2>
    <div class="text">
      <p>A week ago marked 4 years of happy usage of Linear.</p>
      <ZoomableImage
        width="100%"
        src="/images/linear-first-letter.png"
        alt="Linear first letter"
      />
      <p>
        It was love at first sight. I liked the clean and simple design, the
        idea of the app, and the attention to detail. It was Linear that taught
        me that when you move the cursor to the submenu, you need to take into
        account its path and not activate other menu items along the way. I’ve
        never thought about that kind of adjustment for better UX. I haven’t
        dreamed to join the team at that time, but I decided that I want to
        strive to the same level of care about the end user that you guys have.
      </p>
      <p>
        The stars aligned in such a way that I’m looking for a job at exactly
        the same time you have a position. I know that you have incredibly high
        standards, but I would like to try to tell a little about myself and see
        if I fit those standards.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div>
      <h2>About me</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text">
      <p>I'm a frontend engineer with more than 10 years of experience.</p>
      <p>
        I love to design and build web and desktop applications so much that I
        even do it in my free time. To better understand design, I asked my
        designer friend to mentor me.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also like to help other people. I've been a mentor for few people and
        I constantly help other developers with their issues in React and NodeJS
        chats.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div>
    <h2>My personal projects</h2>
  </div>
  <section>
    <div>
      <div class="project-title">
        <img src="/icons/kona.svg" alt="Kona logo" width="32" height="32" />
        <h3>Kona</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="project-info">
        <div>
          <em>2021 - Present</em>
        </div>
        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag">React</span>
          <span class="tag">TypeScript</span>
          <span class="tag">Fastify</span>
          <span class="tag">GraphQL</span>
          <span class="tag">react-hook-form</span>
          <span class="tag">React-DnD</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        This project is started as a way to learn something new that could help
        me on my full-time job, but now it is something very important to me.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of the components (some of which are quite complex) used in this
        project are built by me. For example, the full calendar component uses
        the drag-and-drop technique extensively, and I've spent a lot of time
        making it work correctly. The calendar is also scrollable in each
        direction infinitely, which is not very common for such kinds of
        applications.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section>
    <div>
      <div class="project-title">
        <img src="/images/editor.png" alt="Kona logo" width="38" height="34" />
        <h3>Kona Editor</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="project-info">
        <div>
          <em>2025 - Present</em>
        </div>
        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag">React</span>
          <span class="tag">TypeScript</span>
          <span class="tag">Slate.js</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        I absolutely adore text editors! Text editor was the first project that
        I started building ~20 years ago to learn programming.
      </p>
      <p>
        I've chosen Slate framework for building this project. It's a powerful
        and very complex library, but I've been able to learn a lot from it. All
        the plugins for Kona Editor are built by me.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
